  body: "# Retirement Pension: the older regime in the DMG\n\n## Source-backed proposal\n\nChapter 75 uses RP as
    the legislative term for old State Pension and distinguishes its components and contribution routes from the
    State Pension regime discussed in chapter 74.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\nThe introductory pensionable-age
    boundary does not remove the need to examine category-specific provisions. The source signposts a Category C
    exception and retains historical material. No award or present rate is established here.\n\n## Inspected passages\n\
    \n- [DMG 75001, PDF page 2](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69d8f248eb7e7bc565170231/dmg-Ch-75.pdf#page=2).\n\
    - [DMG 75002, PDF page 2](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69d8f248eb7e7bc565170231/dmg-Ch-75.pdf#page=2).\n\
    - [DMG 75004, PDF page 2](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69d8f248eb7e7bc565170231/dmg-Ch-75.pdf#page=2).\n\
    \n## Provenance and review\n\nIndependent experimental interpretation of DWP guidance, not an official DWP document.
    All definitions and relationships are model-assisted and unreviewed. No individual eligibility, award, legal
    conclusion or executable rule is supplied.\n\nSource observation, listing-page update, printed revision, stated
    legal date and pension event date have separate meanings. PDF page numbers are one-based file positions; extraction
    may damage reading order, footnotes and characters. No visual PDF or specialist acceptance is claimed.\n\n-
    `dmg-vol12-ch75` — PDF SHA-256 `655e7acb31f09f5169efbe40419091ee479f88c0c45b65c7a507b042b67712f9`; page-extraction
    SHA-256 `0d037880d2aeaff1be89235ee987ca4acb1c839fcf1ead8b8be2daa9f6795465`.\n"
